[{"category":"section","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#SimplexInterpolation","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"Documentation for SimplexInterpolation\n\n","title":"SimplexInterpolation"},{"category":"type","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.InterpSimplex","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"struct InterpSimplex\n\nStructure to describe a simplex together with precomputed properties used to determine barycentric coordinates. In N dimensions, given N+1 vertices on a simplex vecx_i and a point veca for which we want to determine the barycentric coordinates alpha_i, it should be satisfied that veca = sum_i=1^N+1alpha_i vecx_i together with the condition sum_i=1^N+1lpha_i = 1 This is equivalent to solving a linear system A\u000beclpha=\u000becb where A=(vecx_1-vecx_N)dots(vecx_N-1-vecx_N)qquad vecb=veca-vecx_N and vecalpha contains th barycentric coordinates from 1 to (N-1). To efficiently determine barycentric coordinates we use StaticArrays with precomputed LU factorizations of the A matrix. We also store the vertex vecx_N separately.\n\npoints: matrix containing the points with dimensions ndims x npoints\nA_lu: factorized matrix in the linear system to determine the barycentric coordinate coefficients\nend_point: Coordinates of vecx_N, used to set up the value of vecb in the linear system when a point veca is provided.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.InterpSimplex"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.InterpSimplex-Tuple{Matrix, Vector{Int64}, Int64}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function InterpSimplex(points)\n\nConstruct a simplex based on the given points. points must be a matrix of dimensions ndims x npoints. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.InterpSimplex"},{"category":"type","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.SimplexInterpolant","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"struct SimplexInterpolant{N,P,LU,E}\n\nStructure containing information on a Delaunay triangulation to perform interpolation.\n\nsimplexes: Instances of Simplex for each of the simplexes in the triangulation\npoints: Points used for the triangulation. points must be a matrix of dimensions ndims x npoints.\npoints_indeces: For each simplex, contains the indeces of the points that compose it. Dimensions are ndims+1 x nsimplexes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.SimplexInterpolant"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.SimplexInterpolant-Tuple{Any}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function SimplexInterpolant(points)\n\nConstructor for a SimplexInterpolant based on a set of points. points must be a matrix of dimensions ndims x npoints. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.SimplexInterpolant"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.barycentric_coords!-Union{Tuple{E}, Tuple{LU}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{N}, Tuple{Any, StarStats.InterpSimplex{N, P, LU, E}, Any, Any}} where {N, P, LU, E}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function barycentric_coords!(point, s::InterpSimplex{N,P,LU,E}, coords, bcache) where {N,P,LU,E}\n\nNon-allocating calculation of barycenter coordinates. Results are stored in place in coords.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.barycentric_coords!"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.barycentric_coords-Union{Tuple{E}, Tuple{LU}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{N}, Tuple{Any, StarStats.InterpSimplex{N, P, LU, E}}} where {N, P, LU, E}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function barycentric_coords(point, s::InterpSimplex{N,P,LU,E}) where {N,P,LU,E}\n\nWrapper for barycentric_coords! that is non-mutating.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.barycentric_coords"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.compute_simplex_interpolation-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function compute_simplex_interpolation(info, values)\n\nGiven the results from the function interpolation_info and the values of a function evaluated in the points used to create the SimplexInterpolant, return the interpolated value. Returns NaN if no simplex contains the point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.compute_simplex_interpolation"},{"category":"method","location":"SimplexInterpolation/#StarStats.interpolation_info-Union{Tuple{V}, Tuple{E}, Tuple{LU}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{N}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{Vector{T}, StarStats.SimplexInterpolant{N, P, LU, E, V}}} where {T, N, P, LU, E, V}","page":"SimplexInterpolation","text":"function interpolation_info(point, si::SimplexInterpolant{N,P,LU,E}) where {N,P,LU,E}\n\nIterate through all simplexes in the SimplexInterpolant si to find the simplex containing the given point. Returns the Barycentric coordinates of the point for the containing simplex, the indeces of the points that form the vertices of the simplex and the id of the simplex. If no simplex is found that contains the point zero values are returned for the indeces and coefficients.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.interpolation_info"},{"category":"section","location":"StellarModelSet/#StellarModelSet","page":"StellarModelSet","text":"Documentation for StellarModelSet\n\n","title":"StellarModelSet"},{"category":"section","location":"SimulationData/#SimulationData","page":"SimulationData","text":"Documentation for SimulationData\n\n","title":"SimulationData"},{"category":"method","location":"SimulationData/#StarStats.mesa_dataframe_loader-Tuple{Any}","page":"SimulationData","text":"mesa_dataframe_loader\n\nFunction \n\nFields:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.mesa_dataframe_loader"},{"category":"section","location":"StellarModelGrid/#StellarModelGrid","page":"StellarModelGrid","text":"Documentation for StellarModelGrid\n\n","title":"StellarModelGrid"},{"category":"type","location":"StellarModelGrid/#StarStats.StellarModelGrid","page":"StellarModelGrid","text":"ModelDataGrid\n\nStruct containing the definition of a grid including the input variables defining it and their values \n\nFields:\n\ndfs: Multidimensional array of DataFrames containing individual evolutionary track information from a grid of models.       This is populated with the load_grid function.    \ninputs: Vector of String vectors containing the parth of the path from a track. (TODO give an example)\ninput_names: Vector of Symbol containing the names of each parameter of the grid.  \ninput_values: Result of parsing the inputs into floats.   \nEEPs: Array of integers representing the Equivelant Evolutionary Points (see Dotter, 2016)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.StellarModelGrid"},{"category":"section","location":"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint/#EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint","page":"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint","text":"Documentation for EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint\n\n","title":"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint"},{"category":"method","location":"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint/#StarStats.compute_distance_and_EEPs!-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint","text":"computedistanceand_EEPs\n\nFunction \n\nFields:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StarStats.compute_distance_and_EEPs!"},{"category":"section","location":"#StarStats.jl","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for StarStats.jl\n\nPages = [\n    \"SimulationData.md\",\n    \"EquivalentEvolutionaryPoint.md\",\n    \"StellarModelGrid.md\",\n    \"SimplexInterpolation.md\",\n    \"StellarModelSet.md\",\n]","title":"StarStats.jl"}]
